a snow-covered bridge buckles and  collapses on friday morning in  pittsburgh  several cars and buses were on the  bridge at the time ten people suffered  minor injuries in an ironic twist just  hours later president joe biden comes to  see it firsthand he's on his way to  deliver a speech nearby remarkably about  america's crumbling infrastructure  eyewitnesses say the bridge collapse  could have been a lot worse if this had  happened 15 to 20 minutes later you  would have had buses with school kids on  it buses with workers  so the timing of this in terms of  happening when it did was very  fortuitous  the bridge was built nearly a half  century ago  like dozens across the city of  pittsburgh  the federal government rated it in poor  condition back in 2011. and more than  three years ago this twitter user  highlighted its corroded steel beams  it's unclear if it had ever been fixed  but it's not just in pittsburgh all over  america infrastructure is in disrepair  and that's why last year congress passed  and president joe biden signed into law  a 1.2 trillion dollar infrastructure  plan  to rebuild everything including railroad  lines airports  tunnels roads  and yes bridges  biden is using the bridge collapse to  champion the urgency of his hard-fought  infrastructure efforts across the  country there are 45 000 bridges in poor  condition  it's just simply unacceptable we have to  do something about this  i've talked about it every time i've  come to pittsburgh  and we finally got it done  according to the american society of  civil engineers in the u.s there are 617  000 bridges 42 percent are over 50 years  old and 46 000 bridges in the u.s are  structurally deficient  on friday the problems with bridges  abundantly clear for everyone to see  gabriel rosando al jazeera new york
 

